### commit
733861d9 fix(weather): the pause after a failure counts from the start of the failed run

Cycles come one cache window apart, start to start, but the pause was
counted from the end of the failed run. Pirate Weather's three tries
(1 s and 2 s apart) take a good 3 s, so at the cap -- a pause of the cache
window, interval minus one second -- the next cycle arrived a couple of
seconds inside the pause and was answered from it; a gate that kept
failing asked only every second cycle, and a recovered service was
noticed up to one cycle late. Seen live on a test install with a 10-minute
interval: the 13:00 cycle got the replay with 2 s of the pause to go.

The backoff now counts from the start of the run, as the cycle does. What a
response asked for with Retry-After still counts from that response, so a
service that named a wait is never asked again early.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

